explicit kind of racism, but the majority of white Americans, because they've grown up in a culture that has been historically racist in many ways, because they're exposed to the media that associates violence, drugs, and poverty with certain groups, most white Americans, the majority of white Americans, about two-thirds to three-quarters, have these unconscious, implicit racial biases. How do people work on getting rid of these biases if they don't know they're biased? That's the biggest challenge because most of us are really well practiced at convincing ourselves that we're not prejudiced. So most of us want to be good people. Prejudice is bad.
即显性的种族主义，但大多数白人美国人，因为他们成长在一个在许多方面历史上都存在种族主义的文化中，因为他们接触的媒体将暴力、毒品和贫困与特定群体联系在一起，大多数白人美国人，大约三分之二到四分之三，都有这种无意识的、内隐的种族偏见。如果人们不知道自己有偏见，他们该如何努力消除这些偏见呢？这是最大的挑战，因为我们大多数人都非常擅长说服自己我们没有偏见。所以我们大多数人都想成为好人。偏见是不好的。

