A lot of it is just about having conversations about race in general, maybe with people who are not your racial or ethnic background. Do you think that that helps sort of uncover these biases that you don't know you have? Yeah. One of the problem with averse of racism that I mentioned before is that you actually avoid the group. Okay. And you avoid the group because they make you uncomfortable, and you can therefore maintain your stereotypes of the group.
其中很大一部分只是关于进行关于种族的对话，也许是与那些不是你种族或族裔背景的人进行对话。你认为这有助于揭示那些你不知道自己拥有的偏见吗？是的。我之前提到的厌恶型种族主义的问题之一是，你实际上是在回避这个群体。好的。你回避这个群体是因为他们让你感到不舒服，因此你可以维持你对该群体的刻板印象。

